# Keep the build context to what the image build actually reads.
#
# Nothing here is needed to produce the image: both stages install from the
# lockfile and build from source, and the version arrives as a build argument, so
# even `.git` is dead weight. A smaller context is a faster and more cacheable
# `COPY . .`.
#
# EVERY PATTERN THAT SHOULD MATCH BELOW THE ROOT NEEDS ITS `**/` FORM. A bare
# `*.tsbuildinfo` matches only at the context root — Docker's matcher does not
# give it gitignore's "any depth" behaviour. That silently cost this image its
# build: the three `tsconfig.tsbuildinfo` files were copied in, `**/dist` was
# correctly excluded, and `tsc -b` — finding a build-info file that said
# everything was up to date and no `dist/` to contradict it — emitted nothing.
# `@homebox/api` then failed with "Cannot find module '@homebox/db'". Bare
# patterns are kept alongside their `**/` form only for readability; the `**/`
# one is what does the work.

.git
.github

# Installed and generated trees — the image builds its own.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo

# Local state: the dev database, uploads, and the model cache.
data
.dev
.worktrees
.claude
.agents
.superpowers
skills-lock.json

# Secrets. The image reads its configuration from the environment at run time.
.env
.env.*

# Test and docs artifacts.
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report
.playwright-mcp
docs
